    "title": "Media‑Rich Profile",
    "description": "Build a page that embeds a responsive image, audio, and video with proper attributes.",
    "estimatedMinutes": 10,
    "problemStatement": "Create an 'About Me' page that showcases multimedia content.\n\n**Requirements:**\n- A **profile picture** using `<figure>` and `<figcaption>`. Use an `<img>` with `src=\"profile.jpg\"`, a descriptive `alt`, and set `width=\"300\" height=\"300\"`.\n- Below the image, add a short **audio introduction**. Use `<audio controls>` with a single `<source>` pointing to `intro.mp3` (type `audio/mpeg`) and fallback text 'Your browser does not support audio.'.\n- Embed a **video** (a hobby showcase) using `<video controls width=\"560\" height=\"315\">`. Include two sources: one `hobby.mp4` (type `video/mp4`) and one `hobby.webm` (type `video/webm`). Add a fallback paragraph: 'Download the <a href=\"hobby.mp4\">MP4</a> instead.' \n- Ensure the video has a `poster=\"hobby-poster.jpg\"`.\n\nAll file paths are relative to the same folder. Write the whole body code (assume the basic skeleton exists).",
    "hints": [
        "Remember to close the `<figure>` after `<figcaption>`.",
        "The `<audio>` element needs `controls` to show the player.",
        "The `<video>` fallback content is placed after the `<source>` tags, inside `<video>`."
    ],
    "expectedOutput": "A body with a figure, an audio player, and a video player, all with proper fallbacks and attributes.",
    "solutionCode": "<h1>About Me</h1>\n\n<figure>\n  <img src=\"profile.jpg\" alt=\"Smiling woman with glasses standing in a park\" width=\"300\" height=\"300\">\n  <figcaption>That's me, enjoying a sunny afternoon!</figcaption>\n</figure>\n\n<h2>Listen to My Intro</h2>\n<audio controls>\n  <source src=\"intro.mp3\" type=\"audio/mpeg\">\n  Your browser does not support audio.\n</audio>\n\n<h2>My Hobby: Sketching Timelapse</h2>\n<video controls width=\"560\" height=\"315\" poster=\"hobby-poster.jpg\">\n  <source src=\"hobby.mp4\" type=\"video/mp4\">\n  <source src=\"hobby.webm\" type=\"video/webm\">\n  <p>Download the <a href=\"hobby.mp4\">MP4</a> instead.</p>\n</video>"
}